perfcached (0.4.0~rc28-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * An apply thread looks before it sleeps: apply_threads = 4 applied 55%
    of the offered load and dropped 27,716 datagrams; it now applies 99%
    and drops 748.
  * mode = eager with [wal] save = off is a data-loss configuration and
    the daemon says so at startup - an eager replica does not persist the
    copies it receives, so only a snapshot makes a whole-fleet outage
    recoverable.
  * The README says which mode to run, and that a replication factor is
    an availability feature rather than a durability one.

